# A numeric name passed to a boxed parameter, in an OBSERVED program.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that `nm[x] == 1` means "inferred numeric", NOT
# "is a live C double" — and the storage regime decides which. Under g_observed
# numeric variables live in the ENV (aot_observe_num), not in C doubles; the
# module decl loop emits no `static double` for them at all, and emit_num's own
# ident arm opens by saying so.
#
# An emit_args arm that boxes `make_num(eig_x)` is therefore right in one regime
# and wrong in the other. Written without the g_observed guard it produced a
# SILENT WRONG VALUE — a frame local declared `double eig_m = 0` and never
# written, because the assignment went to the env:
#
#   VM   hi / 0 / 42 / 0 / 0 / 0
#   AOT  hi / 0 /  0 / 0 / 0 / 0        both rc 0, no diagnostic
#
# and at module scope, where no declaration exists at all, a gcc error on an
# undeclared `eig_m` — the same fault, loud instead of silent, decided only by
# where the name lives.
#
# EVERY OTHER FIXTURE IN THIS FAMILY IS UNOBSERVED, which is why 123/123 stayed
# green. What makes this program observed are the TWO `converged of` calls
# below, and BOTH are load-bearing — one per storage regime, because the two
# failure modes live in different scopes.
#
# Measured against the broken emitter, rather than asserted:
#   delete `converged of q` only          -> STILL FAILS (build, 'eig_top_m')
#   delete `converged of top_q` only      -> STILL FAILS (build, 'eig_top_m')
#   delete BOTH                           -> passes; the fixture is defused
#
# Note what the rows actually show: EITHER trigger alone keeps the whole program
# observed (g_observed is a whole-program flag), so the module-scope failure
# fires in both single-deletion rows and the frame-local failure never shows
# independently. An earlier version of this table labelled row 2 "the
# frame-local half", which was a guess about the mechanism written next to a
# measured result — the verdicts were right and the attribution was invented.
#
# An earlier version of this header said deleting `converged of q` alone
# defuses it. That was wrong, and wrong in the dangerous direction: someone
# checking the claim would have found the fixture still red and concluded the
# guard was fine. A "load-bearing" note is itself a claim and has to be run.

define g(y) as:
    if (type of y) == "str":
        print of y
    else:
        print of (y * 2)
    return 0

define h(k) as:
    # a FRAME local: declared as a C double that is never written under
    # g_observed, so the silent-wrong form
    local m is k + 20
    local s is "hi"
    print of (g of s)
    print of (g of m)
    local q is m
    q is q + 1
    print of (converged of q)
    return 0

print of (h of 1)

# and the MODULE-scope form, which has no declaration at all and failed the
# build rather than answering wrongly
top_s is "hello"
print of (g of top_s)
top_m is 21
print of (g of top_m)
top_q is 1
top_q is 2
print of (converged of top_q)
